{
  "description": "F-CAP: one wrist session end to end, in three cases, shared by both stacks so the wrist's capture and the phone's import are checked against the same numbers. `timeline` is the script: ops apply in array order, the array is ordered by `at`, and a sensor sample (`hr`, `steps`) is applied before any other op at the same instant. `start` creates the session with no modality over `exercises` (no slot declares an effort kind, so kinds derive from capabilities: timed, round, set), and the wrist's entry-id factory yields `entryIds` in order. `dial` sets a metric (a `WatchMetricKey`) to `value`, in seconds or kilograms, before the next `log`; a follow-on round timer is planned at the round length dialled for the round that started it. `pauseRound` and `resumeRound` pause and resume the running round timer. `end` is the wrist's own End; `answer` confirms the effort-rating prompt. `sensorPermissions` says which sensors the case grants. `expectedEvents` are the wrist's observations in store order, timestamps in the wrist's wire form. `expectedImport` is what the phone holds after importing them. `derivation` explains every summary value so the arithmetic can be rechecked by hand.",
