      "derivation": {
        "e-run": "Window 10:00:00-10:20:00: loggedAt minus the dialled 1200 s. HR in the window: 120 (10:05:00), 140 (10:10:00), 160 (10:15:00), so avg 140, max 160. Steps: baseline 0 (no steps sample before 10:00:00); the chain 0 -> 800 -> 1600 -> 3200 (10:20:00, window end inclusive) adds 800 + 800 + 1600 = 3200. The 3300 at 10:30:00 is outside the window.",
        "e-r1": "No round timer is running, so the window is 10:25:00-10:30:00: loggedAt minus the dialled 300 s. HR: 150 (10:26:00), 170 (10:28:00), so avg 160, max 170. The 100 at 10:24:30 is before the window. Rounds carry no steps, even though the steps sample at 10:30:00 lies inside this window and e-r2's.",
        "e-r2": "The follow-on round timer starts at 10:30:00, planned 300 s, and is paused over [10:32:00, 10:34:00), so it completes at 10:37:00; logged at 10:37:05, the window is 10:30:00-10:37:00 and pausedMs is 120000. HR: 150 (10:31:00), 180 (10:36:00), so avg 165, max 180. The 100 at 10:33:00 falls inside the pause and is excluded; including it would give 143.33.",
        "e-r3": "The next round timer starts at 10:37:05, planned 300 s, and completes at 10:42:05; logged at 10:42:10, the window is 10:37:05-10:42:05. HR: 145 (10:37:05, window start inclusive; the sample is applied before e-r2's log at the same instant), 165 (10:40:00), so avg 155, max 165. The 175 at 10:42:08 is after the window end.",
        "e-set1, e-set2, e-set3": "Set events never carry heart rate. Each is 5 reps x 80 kg.",
        "rec-13-rest, rec-15-rest, rec-17-rest": "Every completed rest is its own event (D-219, D-224): the follow-on rest timer a set's log starts, ended by the next log (rec-13-rest 10:45:00-10:48:00, rec-15-rest 10:48:00-10:51:00) or by the finish (rec-17-rest 10:51:00-10:55:00). The id is the rest timer row's record id plus \"-rest\"; loggedAt is the end, and afterEntryId names the effort the rest followed (D-221).",
        "end-s-cap-1 session": "Session window 10:00:00-10:55:00. Fifteen positive samples sum to 2145, so avg 143; max 180. A round's pause is not a session pause, so the 100 at 10:33:00 counts. The 0 at 10:50:00 is a glitch and is ignored.",
        "end-s-cap-1 set block sx-bench/ex-bench": "The span starts at the loggedAt of the latest effort entry logged before e-set1 (e-r3, 10:42:10) and ends at e-set3's loggedAt (10:51:00, inclusive). HR: 110 (10:44:00), 130 (10:47:00), 150 (10:51:00), so avg 130, max 150. The 175 at 10:42:08 is before the span; the 0 at 10:50:00 is ignored.",
        "rating-s-cap-1": "The user answers 4 at 10:55:20."
      }
    },
